Z||000005||zeusrekning||01-16-2001||02:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>There are usually 8-12 Fiero vendors in the Fiero section of the show</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Is this not just a fiero show???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||01-16-2001||07:37 AM||||The show started out as a Mopar show years ago and grew from there.  The Florida Fiero Council thought that a show at that time of year was nice and tagged onto the show as did many other car clubs.  So now you have thousands of cars coming into the track for the show with hundreds of vendors.<P>I did not do a count, but I believe that the Fiero section had the largest single car model at the show.  Nothing else came close as to number of cars of one model present.<P>The same concept applies to the Carlisle show.  It started out as an import/replicar show.  The Fiero has been a major kitcar doner and MidAtlantic Fiero tagged a Fiero show with the Import/Kit car show and has had the largest individual model showing up for the last several years.<P>It makes it nice to have your car participate in a major show..lots of other sites to see.||||reg||3
Z||000007||mrfixit58||01-16-2001||07:57 AM||||This show is HUGE! it covers about 90% of the entire infield at the speedway. If your a car guy, you'll see just about every make and model of American muscle car you can think of. The swap meet area is the biggest in the southeast. If you attend, you won't be dissapointed.<P>Hope to see ya there,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
